From a4b68ad654bedc6b401e648fd359701e62321f79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:54:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] powerpc: build the vDSO after the stack protector flags are
 set

stack_protector_prepare appends the -mstack-protector-guard flags to
KBUILD_CFLAGS with $(eval) from within its recipe, so the flags only
reach commands that make starts after that recipe. vdso_prepare builds
the vDSO from a sibling prerequisite of prepare. Nothing orders the two,
so the vDSO is built with or without the flags depending on the order in
which make starts the recipes.

The vDSO is built with -fno-stack-protector, so its code is the same
either way. GCC records the command line in DW_AT_producer, though, and
the kernel embeds vdso32.so.dbg with its debug information. Two builds
of the same kernel therefore differ:

  -GNU C11 14.4.0 ... -mstack-protector-guard=tls -mstack-protector-guard-reg=r2 -mstack-protector-guard-offset=872 -m32 -g -O2 ...
  +GNU C11 14.4.0 ... -m32 -g -O2 ...

Make vdso_prepare depend on stack_protector_prepare, so the vDSO is
always built with the final KBUILD_CFLAGS.

---
 arch/powerpc/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/powerpc/Makefile
+++ b/arch/powerpc/Makefile
@@ -405,6 +405,7 @@
 
 ifdef CONFIG_STACKPROTECTOR
 prepare: stack_protector_prepare
+vdso_prepare: stack_protector_prepare
 
 PHONY += stack_protector_prepare
 stack_protector_prepare: prepare0
